    <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         ICON GEOMETRIES

         Vector paths, NOT an icon font. Segoe Fluent Icons ships with Windows 11
         only, and this project has already lost a whole session to a Win11-only
         font: naming Segoe UI Variable first sent WPF's fallback resolution into
         infinite recursion and overflowed the stack inside MeasureOverride,
         before the first frame ever rendered. Geometries have no such failure
         mode, and they take the theme stroke brush directly.

         AUTHORING RULES
         - 24 x 24 coordinate space. The Icon control scales and compensates the
           pen so the rendered stroke stays ~1.5 px at any size.
         - Outline only. No fills, no closed shapes that rely on a fill rule.
         - Minimal internal detail: these are read at 16-20 px.
         - Round joins and caps, applied by the Icon control.

         Keyed Icon<Name>Geometry so Icon.Key="<Name>" resolves at runtime, which
         is what lets NavigationItem.Glyph stay a plain string.
         ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

